   "evidence": "run.ts:248-256 at head skips a targeted-only retry only when the check passed, has a null or zero exit code, timed out, or failed confinement. Nothing requires the listed files to account for every failure. With targetedOnly, results.set(original, {...attempt,...}) uses the targeted attempt as the check result, with no full-suite retry (`if (!targetedOnly) full.push(entry)`). queue.ts:454-457: `const result = retries.get(c) ?? c; return !result.ok || ...` so a passing targeted retry clears the check. parseJUnit ignores root and suite counters that no test case accounts for, and Bun leaves load errors out of the JUnit report entirely. Factory gates add a full-suite retry after a targeted pass for exactly this reason. The land path removed that safeguard without putting a completeness check in its place. The CI backstop on Linux narrows the impact but does not cover failures that only happen on macOS or in the local land check."
